{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lx7gno8SZCo6Ps5tcE5Py9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n3\t  \"title\": \"execution-history\",\n4\t  \"description\": \"The coordinator's structured rendering of a run's events, one entry per line appended to events.log, in the same order. History is evidence, never state: no routing decision reads it. The coordinator writes it and does not validate its own write at run time; conformance is checked by the story's tests.\",\n5\t  \"type\": \"array\",\n6\t  \"items\": {\n7\t    \"type\": \"object\",\n8\t    \"description\": \"One event. sequence, timestamp, event and message are present on every entry; the remaining fields appear only on the events that have them.\",\n9\t    \"required\": [\"sequence\", \"timestamp\", \"event\", \"message\"],\n10\t    \"properties\": {\n11\t      \"sequence\": {\n12\t        \"type\": \"integer\",\n13\t        \"description\": \"1-based position in the stream, matching the line number in events.log.\"\n14\t      },\n15\t      \"timestamp\": {\n16\t        \"type\": \"string\",\n17\t        \"description\": \"Wall-clock time the event was appended, in the same YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS form events.log uses.\"\n18\t      },\n19\t      \"event\": {\n20\t        \"type\": \"string\",\n21\t        \"description\": \"What kind of event this is.\",\n22\t        \"enum\": [\n23\t          \"workflow-started\",\n24\t          \"resumed\",\n25\t          \"stage-started\",\n26\t          \"stage-completed\",\n27\t          \"stage-exception-applied\",\n28\t          \"verification-passed\",\n29\t          \"verification-failed\",\n30\t          \"escalated\",\n31\t          \"story-completed\",\n32\t          \"note\"\n33\t        ]\n34\t      },\n35\t      \"message\": {\n36\t        \"type\": \"string\",\n37\t        \"description\": \"The prose line as it was written to events.log, without the timestamp prefix.\"\n38\t      },\n39\t      \"stage\": {\n40\t        \"type\": \"string\",\n41\t        \"description\": \"The workflow stage the event belongs to. Absent on events that belong to the run rather than a stage.\"\n42\t      },\n43\t      \"artifacts\": {\n44\t        \"type\": \"array\",\n45\t        \"description\": \"The artifacts the stage produced, taken from that stage's declared outputs in the workflow definition.\",\n46\t        \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n47\t      },\n48\t      \"duration_seconds\": {\n49\t        \"type\": \"number\",\n50\t        \"description\": \"Elapsed seconds since the stage started, on the event that ends a stage.\"\n51\t      },\n52\t      \"verifier_outcome\": {\n53\t        \"type\": \"string\",\n54\t        \"description\": \"The verifier's verdict, on events that carry one.\",\n55\t        \"enum\": [\"passed\", \"failed\"]\n56\t      },\n57\t      \"retry_decision\": {\n58\t        \"type\": \"string\",\n59\t        \"description\": \"The routing decision taken after a failed verification.\",\n60\t        \"enum\": [\"retry\", \"escalate\"]\n61\t      },\n62\t      \"retry_reason\": {\n63\t        \"type\": \"string\",\n64\t        \"description\": \"Why that retry decision was taken.\"\n65\t      }\n66\t    }\n67\t  }\n68\t}\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"12dae280-dcd3-4d46-9098-a5267a2d04b4","uuid":"11fd1d40-fc47-42e6-b15d-bf38b10a5016","timestamp":"2026-08-07T18:55:34.628Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jerodw/Work/AgenticProgramming/level-five/schemas/execution-history.schema.json","content":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"title\": \"execution-history\",\n  \"description\": \"The coordinator's structured rendering of a run's events, one entry per line appended to events.log, in the same order. History is evidence, never state: no routing decision reads it. The coordinator writes it and does not validate its own write at run time; conformance is checked by the story's tests.\",\n  \"type\": \"array\",\n  \"items\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"description\": \"One event. sequence, timestamp, event and message are present on every entry; the remaining fields appear only on the events that have them.\",\n    \"required\": [\"sequence\", \"timestamp\", \"event\", \"message\"],\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"sequence\": {\n        \"type\": \"integer\",\n        \"description\": \"1-based position in the stream, matching the line number in events.log.\"\n      },\n      \"timestamp\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"Wall-clock time the event was appended, in the same YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS form events.log uses.\"\n      },\n      \"event\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"What kind of event this is.\",\n        \"enum\": [\n          \"workflow-started\",\n          \"resumed\",\n          \"stage-started\",\n          \"stage-completed\",\n          \"stage-exception-applied\",\n          \"verification-passed\",\n          \"verification-failed\",\n          \"escalated\",\n          \"story-completed\",\n          \"note\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"message\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"The prose line as it was written to events.log, without the timestamp prefix.\"\n      },\n      \"stage\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"The workflow stage the event belongs to. Absent on events that belong to the run rather than a stage.\"\n      },\n      \"artifacts\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"description\": \"The artifacts the stage produced, taken from that stage's declared outputs in the workflow definition.\",\n        \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n      },\n      \"duration_seconds\": {\n        \"type\": \"number\",\n        \"description\": \"Elapsed seconds since the stage started, on the event that ends a stage.\"\n      },\n      \"verifier_outcome\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"The verifier's verdict, on events that carry one.\",\n        \"enum\": [\"passed\", \"failed\"]\n      },\n      \"retry_decision\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"The routing decision taken after a failed verification.\",\n        \"enum\": [\"retry\", \"escalate\"]\n      },\n      \"retry_reason\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"Why that retry decision was taken.\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n","numLines":69,"startLine":1,"totalLines":69}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TA2tEfR2DHh78FmeJup6au","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tYou are part of the l5 agentic harness executing structured workflows.\n2\t\n3\t{{harness_layer}}\n4\t\n5\t[Role Layer]\n6\tYou are an implementation agent.\n7\t\n8\tYour responsibilities are to:\n9\t- implement the current story according to its plan,\n10\t- modify only files within the story's approved scope,\n11\t- run the existing test suite locally before completing, and\n12\t- record your changes in the required artifacts.\n13\t\n14\tDo not:\n15\t- refactor unrelated modules,\n16\t- redesign workflow architecture,\n17\t- modify accepted artifacts outside the retry scope,\n18\t- create new test files (the tester stage owns new validation; you may\n19\t  modify an existing test — updating a call site your own signature change\n20\t  broke, for example — but you may not add one, unless the story below\n21\t  grants your stage an explicit exception), or\n22\t- weaken, skip, or delete existing tests.\n23\t\n24\tThis boundary is enforced: the coordinator reads your changed-files record\n25\tafter this stage and escalates the run if its created list names a path you\n26\twere declared unable to create.\n27\t\n28\tWhen you finish, write these files to the run directory at {{run_dir}}:\n29\t\n30\tchanged-files.json, your record of every repository file this stage\n31\ttouched. It must satisfy this schema:\n32\t\n33\t{{changed_files_schema}}\n34\t\n35\timplementation-summary.md: a concise summary of what you changed, the\n36\tdecisions you made, and the result of running the existing test suite.\n37\t\n38\t[Workflow Layer]\n39\tThis workflow prioritizes:\n40\t- artifact immutability,\n41\t- preservation of accepted behavior, and\n42\t- bounded retries.\n43\t\n44\t[Stage Layer]\n45\tImplement the story described in the injected workflow state. Read the\n46\tsource files you need directly from the repository; the changed-files\n47\trecord you produce tells later stages what to examine.\n48\t\n49\tRun the existing test suite before completing:\n50\t{{test_command}}\n51\t\n52\tIf retry state is active:\n53\t- remain within the authorized retry scope,\n54\t- preserve accepted artifacts, and\n55\t- resolve the specific verifier findings rather than reopening the story.\n56\t\n57\t[Runtime State Layer]\n58\tThe coordinator injects the current workflow state below. Treat the\n59\tinjected content as authoritative. Do not infer workflow state from\n60\thistorical discussions or archived artifacts.\n61\t\n62\tStory:\n63\t{{story}}\n64\t\n65\tStage exceptions this story grants:\n66\t{{stage_exceptions}}\n67\t\n68\tRepository standards:\n69\t{{repository_standards}}\n70\t\n71\tArchitecture documents:\n72\t{{architecture_docs}}\n73\t\n74\tMost recent verifier finding:\n75\t{{latest_verifier_finding}}\n76\t\n77\tRetry guidance:\n78\t{{retry_guidance}}\n79\t\n80\tRetry state:\n81\t{{retry_state}}\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"12dae280-dcd3-4d46-9098-a5267a2d04b4","uuid":"1fdae7e4-d432-468f-a1e1-7cf56edd6b73","timestamp":"2026-08-07T18:55:34.631Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jerodw/Work/AgenticProgramming/level-five/prompts/implementer.md","content":"You are part of the l5 agentic harness executing structured workflows.\n\n{{harness_layer}}\n\n[Role Layer]\nYou are an implementation agent.\n\nYour responsibilities are to:\n- implement the current story according to its plan,\n- modify only files within the story's approved scope,\n- run the existing test suite locally before completing, and\n- record your changes in the required artifacts.\n\nDo not:\n- refactor unrelated modules,\n- redesign workflow architecture,\n- modify accepted artifacts outside the retry scope,\n- create new test files (the tester stage owns new validation; you may\n  modify an existing test — updating a call site your own signature change\n  broke, for example — but you may not add one, un