 path, marker, paths in [\n    (\"orchestration/context_assembler.py\",\"workflow_context\",[\"workflows/\",\"rules/\",\"schemas/\"]),\n    (\"orchestration/story_coordinator.py\",\"archive_attempt\",[\"workflows/\",\"schemas/\",\"rules/\",\"prompts/\",\"orchestration/context_assembler.py\"]),\n]:\n    pre, story = bounds(path, marker)\n    print(path, marker, pre[:8], (story or \"WT\")[:8])\n    for p in paths:\n        d=subprocess.run([\"git\",\"diff\",pre,*( [story] if story else []),\"--stat\",\"--\",p],capture_output=True,text=True,check=True).stdout.strip()\n        print(\"   \", p, \"->\", repr(d[:200]))\nEOF"}},{"tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_01JCmQMRPopEucSciTzuQ4hx","tool_input":{"file_path":"/tmp/probe_bounds.py","content":"import subprocess\n\n\ndef revs(path):\n    return subprocess.run(\n        [\"git\", \"log\", \"--format=%H\", \"--\", path],\n        capture_output=True, text=True, check=True).stdout.split()\n\n\ndef src(rev, path):\n    return subprocess.run(\n        [\"git\", \"show\", rev + \":\" + path],\n        capture_output=True, text=True, check=True).stdout\n\n\ndef bounds(path, marker):\n    newer = None\n    for r in revs(path):\n        if marker not in src(r, path):\n            return r, newer\n        newer = r\n    raise SystemExit(\"none\")\n\n\ncases = [\n    (\"orchestration/context_assembler.py\", \"workflow_context\",\n     [\"workflows/\", \"rules/\", \"schemas/\"]),\n    (\"orchestration/story_coordinator.py\", \"archive_attempt\",\n     [\"workflows/\", \"schemas/\", \"rules/\", \"prompts/\",\n      \"orchestration/context_assembler.py\"]),\n]\nfor path, marker, paths in cases:\n    pre, story = bounds(path, marker)\n    print(path, marker, pre[:8], (story or \"WORKING-TREE\")[:8])\n    for p in paths:\n        args = [\"git\", \"diff\", pre]\n        if story:\n            args.append(story)\n        args += [\"--stat\", \"--\", p]\n        d = subprocess.run(args, capture_output=True, text=True, check=True).stdout.strip()\n        print(\"   \", p, \"->\", repr(d[:300]))\n"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Implementation complete. Summary:\n\n**Built the clean-clone check.** New `schemas/clean-clone-result.schema.json`; a `clean_clone` declaration on the verifier stage in `workflows/story-workflow.json`; clone construction, execution, artifact write and routing in `orchestration/story_coordinator.py`; `{{clean_clone_result}}` injection through `context_assembler.py` and `prompts/implementer.md`. The clone is `git clone` from a local path (no network by construction), gets the working tree applied and committed into it, runs the command from the target's `config.yaml`, and lives in a temp directory removed whatever the result. Failure reuses the existing archive → increment → reroute → escalate path; both outcomes go through `append_event`. Both schema inventories updated, still exact set equality.\n\nVerified beyond the suite with a throwaway driver: green-in-both advances with `retry_count` unchanged; failing-only-in-the-clone never reaches the documenter, archives each attempt, reroutes to `implementer`, and escalates at the ceiling naming the check; gitignored files are absent from the clone and the tracked edit is present; the target's `HEAD` and `git status` are unchanged; the scratch clone is gone.\n\n**Two things you should know.**\n\nThe suite is **417 passed, 9 failed**, not green. All nine are in `tests/test_story_011_validation.py`, which this story's `do_not_modify` list forbids me to edit. Its `both_implementations` fixture asserts the current coordinator produces byte-identical `events.log` messages and a run directory differing from the pre-story-011 implementation by exactly one filename — which reads as \"no story may ever add an event or artifact again.\" That is the same over-broad-scope defect commit 3b05b99 fixed one instance of *in that same file*. No implementation choice satisfies it while the shipped workflow declares `clean_clone`; the fix is to bound those assertions to the story-011-era workflow, and that edit is off-limits to me. I left it alone rather than widening my scope.\n\nSeparately, six pre-existing `git diff HEAD` assertions in stories 009 and 010 went red because this story touches `schemas/`, `workflows/`, `prompts/` and `context_assembler.py`. Those files are in scope and not forbidden, so I bounded them at both ends the way 3b05b99 bounded story-011's — strictly stronger, nothing relaxed.\n\nI left `.harness/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` to the documenter: the task list names it, but `likely_file_changes` assigns it `stage: documenter`, and that field exists to settle exactly that question.","ttft_ms":3141,"ttft_stream_ms":2143,"time_to_request_ms":45,"type":"result","duration_ms":748004,"uuid":"4c92b08e-3578-4705-b058-b454e3ec7d5c"}

