k to make a\n154-    routing decision; state.json remains the coordinator's only routing\n155-    source.\n156-    \"\"\"\n157-    stamp = time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\")\n158-    with open(run_dir / \"events.log\", \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as log:\n159-        log.write(f\"[{stamp}] {message}\\n\")\n160-\n161-    history = load_history(run_dir)\n162-    entry: dict = {\n163-        \"sequence\": len(history) + 1,\n164-        \"timestamp\": stamp,\n165-        \"event\": kind,\n166-        \"message\": message,\n167-    }\n168-    optional = {\n169-        \"stage\": stage,\n170-        \"artifacts\": artifacts,\n171-        \"duration_seconds\": duration_seconds,\n172-        \"verifier_outcome\": verifier_outcome,\n--\n465:def archivable_artifacts(stages: list[dict]) -> list[str]:\n466-    \"\"\"Collect every stage artifact name the loaded workflow declares.\n467-\n468-    The union of each stage's outputs, its changed_files record, and the keys\n469-    of its schemas map — the same three places the coordinator already reads\n470-    artifact names from. No artifact name is written here, so a workflow that\n471-    adds a stage artifact gets it archived with no code change. Sorted, so\n472-    the archive is deterministic.\n473-    \"\"\"\n474-    names: set[str] = set()\n475-    for stage in stages:\n476-        names.update(stage.get(\"outputs\", []))\n477-        record = stage.get(\"changed_files\")\n478-        if record:\n479-            names.add(record)\n480-        names.update(stage.get(\"schemas\", {}))\n481-    return sorted(names)\n482-\n483-\n484:def archive_attempt(run_dir: Path, artifacts: list[str], attempt: int) -> list[str]:\n485-    \"\"\"Copy the superseded attempt's artifacts into attempts/attempt-N/.\n486-\n487-    Evidence is not silently overwritten. The live copies stay at the\n488-    run-directory root under their canonical names, where every reader\n489-    expects them; the archive keeps those same names one directory down.\n