{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdovnhEE8VKvsUBkxmaYB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01236Mb2iS2yQ8ak1GQEEeNK","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/jerodw/Work/AgenticProgramming/level-five/.harness/runs/story-014/verification-result.json","content":"{\n  \"status\": \"failed\",\n  \"blocking_issues\": [\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"issue\": \"The full suite does not pass. `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q` reports 9 failed, 466 passed in 50.32s. All nine failures are in tests/test_story_011_validation.py and all trace to one root cause: story-011's `both_implementations` fixture drives the pre-story-011 coordinator (loaded from git history) and the current coordinator over this repository's shipped workflow, which now declares `clean_clone` on the verifier stage. The legacy coordinator predates that key and never runs the check, so on the two shapes that reach a passing verifier the current run carries one extra events.log line ('clean-clone suite passed with the story committed') and one extra run-directory file. Confirmed directly: `assert names(current_root) - names(legacy_root) == {'execution-history.json'}` fails with `'clean-clone-result.json'` as the extra item; the log-message equality fails on the extra line; and run_status/l5-status differ only because they tail that log. The `escalated` and `escalated_without_a_retry` parameters pass, because no clean-clone check runs there. Failing tests: test_events_log_lines_are_byte_identical_to_the_pre_story_format[happy_path, retry_then_pass], test_the_legacy_run_wrote_no_history_and_this_one_did[happy_path, retry_then_pass], test_l5_status_renders_a_run_identically_before_and_after[happy_path, retry_then_pass], test_l5_status_through_the_script_is_unchanged[happy_path, retry_then_pass], test_a_run_whose_history_keeps_disappearing_routes_identically.\",\n      \"location\": \"tests/test_story_011_validation.py (assertions), triggered by workflows/story-workflow.json and orchestration/story_coordinator.py\",\n      \"required_behavior\": \"`.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q` exits zero with no failures, without weakening or skipping any existing assertion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"issue\": \"This blocking issue cannot be cleared by the implementer under story-014's declared scope, so it is a scope conflict rather than an implementation defect, and a bounded retry to the implementer cannot resolve it. The conflict is structural and I confirmed each leg of it: (1) tests/test_story_011_validation.py is listed in story-014's `scope.do_not_modify`; (2) its `harness_root` fixture is the real repository root (tests/conftest.py returns HARNESS_ROOT), so the differential runs read the shipped workflows/story-workflow.json and cannot be pointed at a story-011-era definition without editing that forbidden file; (3) story-014's acceptance criteria require the run directory to contain clean-clone-result.json after any run that reached a passing verifier and require both the pass and the failure to append an event, and its constraints require the check to be unconditional for every story that reaches a passing verifier - so no conforming implementation can leave the current run's log and run directory equal to the legacy run's on those two shapes. Satisfying story-014's criteria and satisfying story-011's differential assertions are mutually exclusive while the declaration ships. Resolving it requires a human scope decision: either authorize bounding story-011's log-and-artifact equality assertions to a story-011-era workflow definition (the same fix commit 3b05b99 already applied to that file's prompt-scope assertion), or change story-014's criteria.\",\n      \"location\": \"story-014 scope.do_not_modify vs. acceptance criteria; tests/test_story_011_validation.py; tests/conftest.py harness_root\",\n      \"required_behavior\": \"Either the retry is authorized to bound tests/test_story_011_validation.py's cross-implementation log and run-directory equality assertions to the story-011-era workflow definition (strengthening, not relaxing, them), or story-014's criteria are amended so the shipped workflow does not declare the check. Until one is chosen, the story cannot both satisfy its criteria and pass the suite.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unverified\": [\n    \"story-014's own run directory contains no clean-clone-result.json. This is expected and not a finding: the running coordinator loaded the workflow definition at run start, before the clean_clone key existed in it, exactly as the story's constraints state. It means the check's end-to-end behavior could not be observed on this run itself.\",\n    \"The clone-construction, routing, cleanup, target-immutability and no-network criteria were verified through the tester's suite (tests/test_story_014_validation.py, 49 tests, all passing, covering the story's stated verification requirements including the HEAD-baseline fixture, the gitignore exclusion, scratch removal after a failing run, the ceiling escalation, and the omitted-declaration case) rather than by my own independent driver run. I did confirm independently that the full suite run - which exercises the clean-clone check repeatedly - left the target repository's HEAD (19ea7a0) and `git status --porcelain` byte-identical to their pre-run values, and that schemas/clean-clone-result.schema.json validates a conforming record through orchestration/schema_validator.py with no ValueError.\",\n    \"The implementer's repairs to tests/test_story_009_validation.py and tests/test_story_010_validation.py were checked for vacuity rather than accepted on description: their markers resolve to ff80849 (story-009) and 2239a23 (story-010), so both assertions now compare a real commit against its parent and remain non-vacuous. Both files are inside story-014's `tests/` modify scope. I did not find these to weaken anything, but I note the change here because it was not requested by the story's task list.\"\n  ],\n  \"retry_recommended\": false\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":169,"cache_read_input_tokens":59241,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":169},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5af011a7-baf0-43ea-8260-32245177ac52","uuid":"02bccc00-63d7-4eea-8b56-50132a70021c","timestamp":"2026-08-07T19:19:43.135Z","request_id":"req_011Cdovng5Ge2P7z6LiDcXaV"}
