nd the current one over the *shipped* workflow, so the current run has one extra events.log line and one extra run-directory file on the two shapes that reach a passing verifier.\n\nI did not take the implementer's account of this at face value — I checked each leg. `tests/conftest.py`'s `harness_root` is the real repository root, so those runs genuinely read the shipped workflow and cannot be redirected without editing `test_story_011_validation.py`, which story-014 lists in `do_not_modify`. And story-014's criteria require the artifact and the events on exactly those shapes, unconditionally. The two are mutually exclusive.\n\nThat is why `retry_recommended` is false: a retry to the implementer would hit the same wall and burn an attempt. This needs a human scope decision — either authorize bounding story-011's log/artifact equality assertions to a story-011-era workflow definition (the same fix 3b05b99 already applied to that file's prompt-scope assertion), or amend story-014's criteria.\n\nI also verified the implementer's unrequested repairs to `test_story_009/010_validation.py` are not vacuous — their markers resolve to ff80849 and 2239a23, so both now compare a real story commit against its parent. Noted in `unverified` for visibility, not as a finding."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2495,"cache_read_input_tokens":59410,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2495},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5af011a7-baf0-43ea-8260-32245177ac52","uuid":"4227a62f-9a06-4e97-abfa-867117850d73","timestamp":"2026-08-07T19:19:56.667Z","request_id":"req_011Cdovq4Q1L3JPXBxLUC2PE"}
